sg-mail (0.1.0-12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reading mail is quick, above all on Microsoft accounts through DavMail
    (David: slow previews, oldest mail fetched first, "127.0.0.1 not
    reachable" on a big Inbox). Measured with the real test account (QA VM):
    - A click shows the text at once and fills in pictures from inside the
      message and the attachments after: a message kept here in 10-200 ms
      (it was 0.5-2.3 s: waited for every inline picture first).
    - Read on the click itself (Outlook's "when the selection changes"); the
      server's \Seen follows in the background (the read delay setting
      still applies when set).
    - The messages beside one opened are fetched ahead (arrow keys).
    - DavMail accounts: Thunderbird's own autosync and "download for
      offline" are off (they held the folder for minutes, oldest included,
      while a click waited: 3-11 s, some 60 s timeouts); SG Mail fetches
      the newest 500 of the last 30 days of Inbox and Sent Items, newest
      first, in batches of five that give way to the person's clicks
      (previews too: a little at a time); a new account's newest mail is
      ready within a minute. Whole messages (no part-by-part fetching),
      IDLE and a check each minute (new mail in ~15 s), three connections.
      Thunderbird no longer fetches in 64 KB chunks (mail.imap.fetch_by_
      chunks: through DavMail each chunk was a round trip to Microsoft).
    - Uncached messages through DavMail: 0.15-1.4 s (Microsoft's own time).
  * The gateway heals itself: Thunderbird's "connection refused / timed out
    at 127.0.0.1" for a gateway is taken by SG Mail, which starts the user
    service again ("Reconnecting to Microsoft…" in the status bar, no
    dialog; Thunderbird's own alert only after three failures in two
    minutes). DavMail runs with -Xmx1g and exits on OutOfMemoryError; the
    unit restarts it always (2 s, at most 20 times in 5 minutes).
  * Gate: davmail-perf (new; 7 mutants), on Thunderbird 140 and 157;
    launcher gate: whole-message fetches.

